.Dd @MAN_DATE@
.Dt GLYPHASTORE_BACKUP_STORE 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm glyphastore_backup_store
.Nd offline backup or restore of a GlyphaStore data directory
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl hV
.Op Fl Fl json
.Op Fl Fl no-scan
.Ar source-data-dir destination-data-dir
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
performs an offline verified copy of a durable data directory (GlyphaStore
.Sy @PROJECT_VERSION@ ) .
.Sy Stop writers first.
The tool takes exclusive locks, verifies the source, creates an empty
destination, copies catalog Segments then
.Pa manifest.glypha ,
syncs, and verifies the destination.
.Pp
Restore uses the same command with the backup as source and a new empty
destination.
.Pp
This offline tool cannot run against a live locked data directory.
For online fenced backup see wire
.Cm BACKUP
/
.Nm Store::backup_to
(still not zero-fence hot I/O).
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl h , Fl Fl help
Show help and exit 0.
.It Fl V , Fl Fl version
Show version and exit 0.
.It Fl Fl json
Emit a stable JSON report on stdout.
.It Fl Fl no-scan
Skip committed Record scans during source/destination verify.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It 0
Success.
.It 1
Validation, copy, or I/O failure.
.It 2
Usage error.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr glyphastore 7 ,
.Xr glyphastore_verify_store 1 ,
.Xr glyphastored 8
.Pp
Source docs:
.Pa docs/architecture/backup-restore.md .
.Sh AUTHORS
GlyphaStore contributors.
